>> title: Fattoush
>> category: Salads
>> tags: salad, lebanese, sumac, pita, pomegranate molasses
>> counters: Shawarma Counter, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: fattoush, fatoush, fattoosh, fattush, bread salad, Lebanese bread salad, pita salad, sumac salad
>> pairs-with: pomegranate-molasses, tabbouleh, pita-bread
>> servings: 4
>> time: 30 min
>> step.1: fry the pita in oil until brittle
>> step.2: whisk the sumac dressing
>> step.3: cut the vegetables in rough chunks
>> step.4: dress the vegetables, stand 5 min
>> step.5: throw the bread in last, go straight to the table

Fry @day-old pita bread{2}(torn into thumbnail pieces) in @olive oil{3%Tbs}(45 mL) in a #skillet{} over medium heat ~fry{4%min}, turning constantly, until every piece is brittle and deep gold, then drain them on paper.

Whisk @lemon juice{3%Tbs}(45 mL), @ground sumac{1%Tbs}(7 g), @pomegranate molasses{2%tsp}(10 mL), @garlic{1%clove}(grated), @extra-virgin olive oil{1/4%cup}(60 mL), @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp} together until it thickens slightly.

Cut @Persian cucumbers{3}(300 g), @ripe tomatoes{3%medium}(400 g), @radishes{6}, @scallions{4} and @romaine heart{1} into rough half-inch chunks and tear @flat-leaf parsley{1%cup} and @fresh mint{1/2%cup} in with them.

Toss @&(~1)chopped vegetables{} with @&(~2)dressing{} and let them ~stand{5%min}, so the sumac and salt pull a little juice out of the tomatoes and it joins the dressing.

Throw @&(~4)fried pita{} through @&(~1)dressed vegetables{} at the very last moment and take the bowl straight to the table.
